[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/comments/388256406","html_url":"https://github.com/google/ExoPlayer/issues/4238#issuecomment-388256406","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/4238","id":388256406,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM4ODI1NjQwNg==","user":{"login":"ojw28","id":7881572,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4ODE1NzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7881572?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28","html_url":"https://github.com/ojw28","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2018-05-11T04:28:19Z","updated_at":"2018-05-11T04:28:19Z","body":"I think that your solution of posting the call to `setPlayer(null)` will work reliably without the 1000ms delay. Just posting with zero delay should be sufficient. This is because I don't think it's really a race condition as such. I think everything is on a single thread, that it's just an ordering problem, and that posting the call will get the operations into the correct order.\r\n\r\nIn terms of making it so that posting the call isn't necessary, we could probably add checks for `player == null` in `PlayerNotificationManager.PlayerListener`. It's likely we need to do the same thing in `MediaSessionConnector` as well.\r\n\r\nLonger term, this issue could be avoided by having the player pass itself to all listener methods, so `PlayerNotificationManager` could use the passed instance rather than relying on its own player reference.\r\n\r\nMarking this as a bug, probably to add the null checks, however I think it should be pretty straightforward for you to work around the issue, as described above.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/comments/388256406/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"ojw28","id":7881572,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4ODE1NzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7881572?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28","html_url":"https://github.com/ojw28","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"id":1621167751,"node_id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDE2MjExNjc3NTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/events/1621167751","actor":{"login":"ojw28","id":7881572,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4ODE1NzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7881572?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28","html_url":"https://github.com/ojw28","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/following{/oth